1
00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:09,890
A fence is built from wooden pieces.

2
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:12,350
1 panel uses 4 pieces of wood.

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,580
2 panels use 7.

4
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:15,440
3 panels use 10.

5
00:00:15,490 --> 00:00:18,190
How many pieces of wood for 10 panels?

6
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:21,910
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,460
Each new panel adds 3 pieces.

8
00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:30,600
From 3 panels to 10 panels is 7 more panels, so 7 times 3 more pieces.

9
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:32,650
10 plus 21 is 31.

10
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:36,680
Can we find a rule that works for any number of panels?

11
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:41,790
Remember: in 6, 11, 16, 21, the difference is 5 each time.

12
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:44,370
So the next term is 26.

13
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:47,210
The difference tells you the multiplier.

14
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:51,250
The pieces go up by 3, so the rule has 3 times n.

15
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:55,120
Compare: 3 times 1 is 3, but the first term is 4.

16
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:55,830
So add 1.

17
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:58,200
The rule is 3 n plus 1.

18
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:04,440
It fits the picture: each panel adds 3 pieces, plus 1 extra piece at the start.

19
00:01:04,490 --> 00:01:05,260
Your turn.

20
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:07,800
Find the rule for 2, 8, 14, 20.

21
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:11,410
Pause the video and try it.

22
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:14,420
The difference is 6, so start with 6 n.

23
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:17,500
6 times 1 is 6, but the first term is 2.

24
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:18,580
So subtract 4.

25
00:01:18,630 --> 00:01:20,980
The rule is 6 n minus 4.

26
00:01:21,030 --> 00:01:22,500
Here is the method.

27
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:27,130
Step 1: count the terms for patterns 1, 2, 3 and 4.

28
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:29,130
Step 2: find the difference.

29
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:32,680
If it is constant, the sequence is linear.

30
00:01:32,730 --> 00:01:37,300
Step 3: compare with d times n, and add or subtract to fit.

31
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:42,440
Step 4: check with another term, and link the rule to the pattern.

32
00:01:42,490 --> 00:01:45,360
Find the rule for 20, 17, 14, 11.

33
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:50,940
The difference is negative 3, so start with negative 3 n.

34
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:54,440
When n is 1, negative 3 n is negative 3.

35
00:01:54,490 --> 00:01:56,010
To get 20, add 23.

36
00:01:56,060 --> 00:01:58,750
The rule is 23 minus 3 n.

37
00:01:58,800 --> 00:01:59,640
Your turn.

38
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:02,600
Find the rule for 30, 26, 22, 18.

39
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:05,970
Pause and work it out.

40
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,480
The difference is negative 4.

41
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:11,330
Negative 4 times 1 is negative 4.

42
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:12,880
To get 30, add 34.

43
00:02:12,930 --> 00:02:15,590
The rule is 34 minus 4 n.

44
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,070
Is 100 a term of 3 n plus 1?

45
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,550
Set 3 n plus 1 equal to 100.

46
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,210
3 n equals 99, so n equals 33.

47
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:25,960
That is a whole number, so yes.

48
00:02:26,010 --> 00:02:28,280
It is the 33rd term.

49
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:31,330
Dots are arranged in squares: 1, 4, 9, 16.

50
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:35,620
Each pattern is n dots by n dots, so the rule is n squared.

51
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:37,990
Not every rule is linear.

52
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:41,270
Jack finds the rule for 7, 12, 17, 22.

53
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:44,240
Which line goes wrong first?

54
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:45,390
Line 2 is wrong.

55
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:48,740
The difference is the number that multiplies n.

56
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:51,080
It should start with 5 n.

57
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:55,150
5 times 1 is 5, and the first term is 7, so add 2.

58
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:57,570
The rule is 5 n plus 2.

59
00:02:57,620 --> 00:03:00,040
A farmer builds a straight fence.

60
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:04,170
Each section is 3 metres long, with a post at each end.

61
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:09,370
1 section needs 2 posts, 2 sections need 3, 3 sections need 4.

62
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:11,440
The rule is n plus 1 posts.

63
00:03:11,490 --> 00:03:14,880
So a 30 section fence needs 31 posts, not 30.

64
00:03:14,930 --> 00:03:18,950
Forgetting the extra post is a famous mistake!

65
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,330
One last question.

66
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,390
Is 62 a term of 6 n plus 2?

67
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:25,860
Pause the video and choose.

68
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:30,690
6 n plus 2 equals 62, so 6 n equals 60, and n equals 10.

69
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,680
A whole number, so yes.

70
00:03:32,730 --> 00:03:34,950
It is the 10th term.

71
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,060
To remember: a constant difference d means a linear sequence.

72
00:03:39,110 --> 00:03:41,160
The rule is d n plus c.

73
00:03:41,210 --> 00:03:45,230
Find c by comparing d times 1 with the first term.

74
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,740
Check with another term.

75
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:50,280
Link the rule to the pattern.

76
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:55,470
Great work! Now practise lesson 9.2 on Camday.
